# Stage A of the split Hazard3 build: lower the *Sail specification alone* and
# cache the result as RTLIL.  See BRINGUP.md, "Cached spec elaboration".
#
# The specification is fixed (build/ibexspec.sv is generated once from the Sail
# model and never changes when the harness is edited), so the expensive
# word-level lowering of it -- proc + opt_muxtree_2, ~7 of the ~16 minutes of
# the monolithic build -- is done here once and reused.
#
# Everything downstream of `flatten` in build_h3_fast.ys is left alone: this
# script deliberately stops before memory_nordff/setundef/expose so that every
# pass which has to see the *whole* design still sees the whole design.
#
# LOWRISC_SAIL_SRC is substituted by the Makefile.

read_slang --top spec_api -DSYNTHESIS -DYOSYS \
	build/ibexspec.sv spec/stub.sv spec/spec_api.sv \
	-I LOWRISC_SAIL_SRC/lib/sv/ \
	--single-unit --no-proc

# Same as the monolithic script: keep all named wires so nothing is optimised
# away before `expose` gets to see it.
setattr -set keep 1 n:\\*
# ...except spec_api's own port wires.  In the monolithic build slang elaborates
# spec_api straight into `top`, so no `spec_api_i.<port>` alias wires exist.
# Here yosys's `flatten` will create them; leaving them un-kept lets the
# opt_clean right after flatten collapse them away again, so the exposed signal
# set matches the monolithic build exactly.
setattr -unset keep i:* o:*

proc
opt_muxtree_2
opt_clean

setattr -unset top
stat
write_rtlil build/spec.il
